{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XDXRXtVmLkh7cMjiAcy2ND","type":"tool_result","content":"326\t### 5.3 Pending (content rows)\n327\t\n328\tOne kind, `:pending`, whose first slot is the reason and whose remaining\n329\tslots are fixed per reason. The reasons are UCF §7.4.3's closed union as\n330\tthe amendment r5 required-keys list fixes them; `:park` and\n331\t`:call-effect` are not reasons and refuse as `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n332\t\n333\t| reason | slots after the reason |\n334\t|---|---|\n335\t| `:next` | `cursor-cell-C` |\n336\t| `:put` | `stream-cref  value-V  op-id-D` |\n337\t| `:ffi` | `cursor-cell-C  call-id-D  op` (op may be nil) |\n338\t| `:ffi-request` | `call-id-D  envelope-V  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  response-cursor-cell-C  op-id-D` |\n339\t| `:link-request` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C  envelope-D  op-id-D` |\n340\t| `:link-response` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C` |\n341\t| `:install` | `name-S` |\n342\t\n343\tThe retained FFI request's `envelope-V` is the complete envelope map,\n344\trecursively encoded under §4's ordinary rules: `[:lit m]` when it\n345\treaches no reference (the common case, arguments such as `[1 2]`), a\n346\t`:map` row otherwise. Lower decodes it and retries it verbatim; it\n347\tnever recomputes the arguments. Correlation must agree, not merely be present:\n348\ta cursor cell's `:cursor-cell-body` stream is the pending's response stream; an\n349\tenvelope's link id or call id equals the pending's; a `:link-request`\n350\tenvelope names the pending's module. `op-id` is `{:yin.k/occurrence P :yin.k/seq n}` as plain data or nil,\n351\tpresent exactly when the write was first attempted through a fenced\n352\twriter, carried verbatim, never minted or renumbered by lift or lower,\n353\tand subject to every rule of §7.4.3 r5 (below the root's\n354\t`:yin.k/next-op-seq`, unique across the task and its children, absent\n355\twhen the body has no origin). `request-envelope` and `envelope` are the\n356\tretained requests, retried verbatim. `call-id` and `link-id` are plain.\n357\tAn `:install` pending is never sufficient alone: the root's installs\n358\tslot must hold the entry for `name`, else lift refuses\n359\t`:yin.k/non-portable` kind `:incomplete-install` and a body carrying it\n360\tis `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n361\t\n362\t### 5.4 Task context (content rows)\n363\t\n364\t| Kind | Slots |\n365\t|---|---|\n366\t| `:store` | `k₁ V₁ k₂ V₂ …` sorted by key; the isolated slice of UCF §7.6.2 |\n367\t| `:module-store` | `manifest-M  store-cref` |\n368\t| `:parked-table` | `P₁ state-cref₁ P₂ state-cref₂ …` sorted by P (each state an `:act` or a `:tail`) |\n369\t| `:install` | `name-S  phase  parent-D  response-D  child-cref` |\n370\t| `:cursor-cells` | the census, §3 |\n371\t| `:cursor-cell-body` | `stream-cref  position` (position in the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` portable cursor domain) |\n372\t\n373\tValidation of a parked state reads decoded task context, never an\n374\tengine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the task's live\n375\t`:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n376\t`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\n377\tsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n378\t`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\n379\t\n380\tResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\n381\tthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\n382\tM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\n383\tsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\n384\treachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n385\t§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\n386\tcontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\n387\tchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\n388\tmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\n389\tthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\n390\tid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\n391\tis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\n392\tcontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\n393\tamendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n394\t**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13; continuation §5.2 B1, §7.2):** the\n395\tmerged lower (`rows/check-install!`) verifies, before any attachment:\n396\tthe phase is one of `#{:running :parked}` (`:install-phase`); the\n397\tresponse is a map with `:status :ok`, a `:manifest` whose\n398\t`:yin.module/name` is the row's module and whose `:yin.module/exports`\n399\tis a collection of symbols, and an `:image` map whose `:value` the\n400\treceiving kernel's loader admits (`:install-response`); and the carried\n401\tchild task's kind is `:blocked` (`:install-child`), the only kind the\n402\tengine retains at a safepoint (a halted or parked child is linked in the\n403\tsweep it halts in, so phase `:running` is a wire phase the codec accepts\n404\tbut the engine never exposes at a safepoint). The link-id-equals-parent\n405\tand image-address-equals-manifest checks of the paragraph above are\n406\t**not** implemented (continuation §11 Q3).\n407\t\n408\t### 5.5 The root\n409\t\n410\t```clojure\n411\t[T :task\n412\t   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\n413\t   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\n414\t   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\n415\t   role             ; :root | :child\n416\t   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\n417\t   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\n418\t   store-cref\n419\t   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\n420\t   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\n421\t   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\n422\t   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\n423\t   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \"v4\" vectors verified to hash to their key\n424\t   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\n425\t   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\n426\t   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\n427\t   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\n428\t   custody]         ; plain, see below\n429\t```\n430\t\n431\t(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\n432\t`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\"v4\"` canonical vectors,\n433\t`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\n434\tthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\n435\t\n436\tKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\n437\tparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\n438\tnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\n439\tneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\n440\tnever collapsed to one; a task with an empty ready queue may hold several\n441\tordered waits.\n442\t\n443\t`custody` is the custody arm carried as plain data, under the rules of\n444\t§7.2.1 and amendment §3, by role, kind and policy:\n445\t\n446\t| role | kind | policy | `custody` |\n447\t|---|---|---|---|\n448\t| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n449\t| root | blocked / parked | fork | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork}` |\n450\t| root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n451\t| root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n452\t| child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n453\t\n454\tThe explicit fork policy spelling projects onto the amendment's\n455\tempty-header fork representation: a fork root proposes nothing and is\n456\tnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n457\t`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. Admission semantics are the governing ones\n458\tunchanged; only the spelling is new. No body carries an epoch.\n459\t\n460\tThe root is a content row and **its id is the transported state's\n461\taddress**, the `B` of UCF §7.3.4 for this carrier. Occurrence and origin\n462\tare inside it, as the governing rule keeps them (§10.1). The code map is\n463\tplain data in the root rather than a row kind: each instruction vector\n464\tkeeps its own address `A` computed exactly as UCF §7.3.2 computes it, and\n465\tthe carrier verifies, never recomputes, that address.\n466\t\n467\t## 6. Canonical cursor-cell numbering\n468\t\n469\tCursor-cell ids must be a function of the state, or two lifts of one state give\n470\ttwo root ids. Local rules are not enough: a cursor cell's number must depend on"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"61b1d883-61cd-4a58-806a-567abc9e9c1b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:16:25.168Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/docs/design/yin.vm.ucf-transport-tuples.md","content":"### 5.3 Pending (content rows)\n\nOne kind, `:pending`, whose first slot is the reason and whose remaining\nslots are fixed per reason. The reasons are UCF §7.4.3's closed union as\nthe amendment r5 required-keys list fixes them; `:park` and\n`:call-effect` are not reasons and refuse as `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n\n| reason | slots after the reason |\n|---|---|\n| `:next` | `cursor-cell-C` |\n| `:put` | `stream-cref  value-V  op-id-D` |\n| `:ffi` | `cursor-cell-C  call-id-D  op` (op may be nil) |\n| `:ffi-request` | `call-id-D  envelope-V  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  response-cursor-cell-C  op-id-D` |\n| `:link-request` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C  envelope-D  op-id-D` |\n| `:link-response` | `link-id-D  name-S  request-stream-cref  response-stream-cref  cursor-cell-C` |\n| `:install` | `name-S` |\n\nThe retained FFI request's `envelope-V` is the complete envelope map,\nrecursively encoded under §4's ordinary rules: `[:lit m]` when it\nreaches no reference (the common case, arguments such as `[1 2]`), a\n`:map` row otherwise. Lower decodes it and retries it verbatim; it\nnever recomputes the arguments. Correlation must agree, not merely be present:\na cursor cell's `:cursor-cell-body` stream is the pending's response stream; an\nenvelope's link id or call id equals the pending's; a `:link-request`\nenvelope names the pending's module. `op-id` is `{:yin.k/occurrence P :yin.k/seq n}` as plain data or nil,\npresent exactly when the write was first attempted through a fenced\nwriter, carried verbatim, never minted or renumbered by lift or lower,\nand subject to every rule of §7.4.3 r5 (below the root's\n`:yin.k/next-op-seq`, unique across the task and its children, absent\nwhen the body has no origin). `request-envelope` and `envelope` are the\nretained requests, retried verbatim. `call-id` and `link-id` are plain.\nAn `:install` pending is never sufficient alone: the root's installs\nslot must hold the entry for `name`, else lift refuses\n`:yin.k/non-portable` kind `:incomplete-install` and a body carrying it\nis `:yin.k/undecodable`.\n\n### 5.4 Task context (content rows)\n\n| Kind | Slots |\n|---|---|\n| `:store` | `k₁ V₁ k₂ V₂ …` sorted by key; the isolated slice of UCF §7.6.2 |\n| `:module-store` | `manifest-M  store-cref` |\n| `:parked-table` | `P₁ state-cref₁ P₂ state-cref₂ …` sorted by P (each state an `:act` or a `:tail`) |\n| `:install` | `name-S  phase  parent-D  response-D  child-cref` |\n| `:cursor-cells` | the census, §3 |\n| `:cursor-cell-body` | `stream-cref  position` (position in the `:dao.stream.remote/v1` portable cursor domain) |\n\nValidation of a parked state reads decoded task context, never an\nengine: the table key `P` and the set of call ids the task's live\n`:ffi`/`:ffi-request` pendings carry are the `task` input of\n`frame/defect` (continuation §3.1), under which an `:act` at a `:park`\nsite is an explicit park and an `:act` at an `:ffi-call` site or a\n`:tail` at a tail call under a live call id is FFI bookkeeping.\n\nResource entries never appear in `:store`; streams and cursor cells lower into\nthe receiver's private resource table beside the program store (linker\nM4, `yin.vm.linker.md` 7.3). `:module-store` rows are the per-module\nsnapshots of §7.6.2's M4 paragraph. The parked table holds exactly the\nreachable records. An `:install` row carries the complete entry of\n§7.4.3 r5: phase `:running` or `:parked`, parent link id (nil where the\ncontract permits), the response verbatim as structural data, and the\nchild as a cref to a whole `:task` row in the child role. \"Verified\"\nmeans verified by the **receiver**, never trusted because it decodes:\nthe response's manifest names the module the row is keyed by, its link\nid equals `parent`, its image is well formed, hashes to the address it\nis delivered under, is the image the manifest names, and its format,\ncontract and the child's profile agree (`yin.vm.linker.md` §5, §9;\namendment §2). A failure is `:yin.k/undecodable` naming the row.\n**Amended after 6b (2026-10-13; continuation §5.2 B1, §7.2):** the\nmerged lower (`rows/check-install!`) verifies, before any attachment:\nthe phase is one of `#{:running :parked}` (`:install-phase`); the\nresponse is a map with `:status :ok`, a `:manifest` whose\n`:yin.module/name` is the row's module and whose `:yin.module/exports`\nis a collection of symbols, and an `:image` map whose `:value` the\nreceiving kernel's loader admits (`:install-response`); and the carried\nchild task's kind is `:blocked` (`:install-child`), the only kind the\nengine retains at a safepoint (a halted or parked child is linked in the\nsweep it halts in, so phase `:running` is a wire phase the codec accepts\nbut the engine never exposes at a safepoint). The link-id-equals-parent\nand image-address-equals-manifest checks of the paragraph above are\n**not** implemented (continuation §11 Q3).\n\n### 5.5 The root\n\n```clojure\n[T :task\n   version          ; 3                       (gated first, §8)\n   contract         ; {:yin.code/contract \"v4\" :yin.k/version 1}, the one profile map (§2)\n   kind             ; :blocked | :parked | :halted\n   role             ; :root | :child\n   id-counter       ; N                       (UCF §7.6.3)\n   free-env-cref    ; a :bindings row, the task's initial free environment (continuation §6.3)\n   store-cref\n   module-stores    ; crefs sorted by M\n   parked-cref      ; :parked-table\n   cursor-cells-cref       ; :cursor-cells census\n   requires         ; plain: UCF §7.6.1's map plus :yin.k/trees (continuation §6.1)\n   code             ; plain: {A canonical-vector …}, \"v4\" vectors verified to hash to their key\n   installs         ; crefs to :install rows, sorted by module name\n   frames           ; crefs to :wait rows, IN WAIT ORDER   (:blocked, :parked)\n   parked-id        ; P or nil                              (:parked only)\n   result           ; V or nil                              (:halted only)\n   custody]         ; plain, see below\n```\n\n(Root replaced 2026-10-11 by continuation §2.6: `free-env-cref` added,\n`contract` is the one profile map, `code` holds `\"v4\"` canonical vectors,\n`requires` gains `:yin.k/trees`.) No `layout` slot and no native image:\nthose were the positional profiles' (v2 amendment §2, §4.1).\n\nKind rules are §7.2.1's: `:blocked` has nonempty frames and neither\nparked-id nor result; `:parked` has frames (possibly empty), a parked-id\nnaming a key of the parked table, no result; `:halted` has a result and\nneither frames nor parked-id. Frames restore in carried order and are\nnever collapsed to one; a task with an empty ready queue may hold several\nordered waits.\n\n`custody` is the custody arm carried as plain data, under the rules of\n§7.2.1 and amendment §3, by role, kind and policy:\n\n| role | kind | policy | `custody` |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| root | blocked / parked | exclusive | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/exclusive :yin.k/occurrence :yin.k/arbitration :yin.k/next-op-seq}` plus `:yin.k/origin` on every successor, absent on a first export |\n| root | blocked / parked | fork | `{:yin.k/policy :yin.k/fork}` |\n| root | halted | exclusive | `{:yin.k/origin …}` only: a result is not a lease subject |\n| root | halted | fork | nil: a fork halt has no custody data and a first fork halt has no origin to carry |\n| child | any | — | nil; validated with its root's occurrence, origin and counter passed down |\n\nThe explicit fork policy spelling projects onto the amendment's\nempty-header fork representation: a fork root proposes nothing and is\nnever upgraded to custody; an exclusive-only receiver refuses it as\n`:yin.k/profile-mismatch`. Admission semantics are the governing ones\nunchanged; only the spelling is new. No body carries an epoch.\n\nThe root is a content row and **its id is the transported state's\naddress**, the `B` of UCF §7.3.4 for this carrier. Occurrence and origin\nare inside it, as the governing rule keeps them (§10.1). The code map is\nplain data in the root rather than a row kind: each instruction vector\nkeeps its own address `A` computed exactly as UCF §7.3.2 computes it, and\nthe carrier verifies, never recomputes, that address.\n\n## 6. Canonical cursor-cell numbering\n\nCursor-cell ids must be a function of the state, or two lifts of one state give\ntwo root ids. Local rules are not enough: a cursor cell's number must depend on","numLines":145,"startLine":326,"totalLines":993}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01XDXRXtVmLkh7cMjiAcy2ND","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
