{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ba3cYADtDTP8in24tRtf8p","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant\n2\t  \"Offers, grants and epoch bindings of M-next C slice C5, and the\n3\t   reclaims, epochs and reopen of slice C6 (UCF 7.7.2, 7.7.7, 7.7.8;\n4\t   docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 14.2.2 and 14.2.3).\n5\t\n6\t   `offer!` admits one snapshot variant of an occurrence: it inspects\n7\t   the bytes (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint), stores the accepted body in a\n8\t   content store, and only then commits the offer fact with its\n9\t   operation baseline, so the ledger never references missing content.\n10\t   An uninspectable body commits nothing and stores nothing.  An offer\n11\t   of a recorded variant is a replay; a known occurrence offered with\n12\t   another origin, or a variant with another baseline, is refused.\n13\t\n14\t   The grant is the dao.lease judge's, composed per plan 1.3:\n15\t   `judge-config` supplies the judge's `:writer`, a ledger adapter that\n16\t   records an appended `:dao.lease/accepted` fact and its `:yin.k/bound`\n17\t   binding as one transaction; its `:reclaim`, a readiness check that\n18\t   revokes nothing; and its `:answer` hook, which grants one proposal per\n19\t   offered, unheld occurrence and refuses the losing candidates.\n20\t   `step!` runs a whole judge-step under the authority's lock, so the\n21\t   hook and the writer see one projection.  The writer, not the hook,\n22\t   enforces one live lease per occurrence.\n23\t\n24\t   The reclaim adapter contract (plan 1.3).  The judge marks a due lease\n25\t   pending and calls `:reclaim`, which only reports readiness; the\n26\t   revocation is the writer's lapse transaction, which holds the\n27\t   `:dao.lease/lapsed` fact and its occurrence's epoch change\n28\t   (`:yin.k/reclaimed`) together.  Nothing claiming the revocation\n29\t   leaves the authority before that transaction commits: until then the\n30\t   projection shows the lease live at its epoch.  A non-ok writer answer\n31\t   leaves the lease pending in the judge and the projection unchanged,\n32\t   and the ledger fold refuses a lapse without its epoch change.\n33\t\n34\t   `reopen!` is plan 1.5 steps 1 to 4 and 6: it opens the authority and\n35\t   reclaims every tenure the ledger shows live, cause :policy, each as\n36\t   one transaction, before it hands the authority out; nothing is\n37\t   regranted.  `rebuild-judge` is step 5: the judge's `:seen` and\n38\t   `:answered` from the ledger, its `:ledger` and `:queue` empty.\n39\t\n40\t   Slice C8 (yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion) hooks in three places: a\n41\t   release lapse of a reported lease carries the closure and its edge,\n42\t   a closed occurrence is never granted, and a successor's offer waits\n43\t   for its predecessor's completion.\"\n44\t  (:require [dao.lease :as lease]\n45\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n46\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n47\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n48\t            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n49\t            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n50\t            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n51\t\n52\t\n53\t(defn- reply\n54\t  ([s] {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status s}})\n55\t  ([s reason o]\n56\t   {::authority/reply (cond-> {:yin.k/status s :yin.k/reason reason}\n57\t                        (some? o) (assoc :yin.k/occurrence o))}))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t;; =============================================================================\n61\t;; Offers\n62\t;; =============================================================================\n63\t\n64\t(defn- offer-decision\n65\t  \"Decide the offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` on `medium`\n66\t   against projection p.\"\n67\t  [address medium b]\n68\t  (fn [p]\n69\t    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence b)\n70\t          known (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n71\t          succession (when-not known (completion/offer-refusal p address b))]\n72\t      (cond\n73\t        (or (:yin.k/fork b)\n74\t            (not (contains? #{:blocked :parked} (:yin.k/kind b))))\n75\t        (reply :refused :not-offerable nil)\n76\t        (not (custody/occurrence? o))\n77\t        (reply :refused :malformed-occurrence nil)\n78\t        (not= (:arbitration p)\n79\t              (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n80\t        (reply :refused :foreign-arbitration o)\n81\t        (nil? medium) (reply :refused :missing-medium o)\n82\t        (contains? (:yin.k/variants known) address)\n83\t        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed :yin.k/occurrence o}}\n84\t        (and known (not= (:yin.k/origin b)\n85\t                         (get-in known [:yin.k/baseline :yin.k/origin])))\n86\t        (reply :refused :occurrence-conflict o)\n87\t        (and known (not= b (:yin.k/baseline known)))\n88\t        (reply :refused :variant-conflict o)\n89\t        succession (reply :refused succession o)\n90\t        :else\n91\t        {::authority/facts [(custody/offer o address medium b)]\n92\t         ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed :yin.k/occurrence o}}))))\n93\t\n94\t\n95\t(defn- store!\n96\t  \"Put the body's bytes in the content store; true once it holds them.\"\n97\t  [store address bytes]\n98\t  (try\n99\t    (contains? #{:inserted :present}\n100\t               ((:put-bytes-fn store) address bytes))\n101\t    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n102\t      false)))\n103\t\n104\t\n105\t(defn offer!\n106\t  \"Admit the offer of the body whose canonical bytes are `bytes` at\n107\t   segment address `address`, carried on `medium`.  `store` is a dao.jing\n108\t   byte-store handle (`:put-bytes-fn`), where the accepted body is put\n109\t   before the ledger references it.  Answers\n110\t\n111\t     {:yin.k/status :committed :yin.k/occurrence o :dao.space/t t}\n112\t     {:yin.k/status :replayed :yin.k/occurrence o}   ; a recorded variant\n113\t     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r ...}\n114\t     {:yin.k/status :suspended :yin.k/reason :content-unavailable}\n115\t\n116\t   with r one of :uninspectable (carrying the inspector's refusal under\n117\t   `:yin.k/inspection`), :not-offerable (a halted root), :malformed-\n118\t   occurrence, :foreign-arbitration, :missing-medium,\n119\t   :occurrence-conflict (another origin) and :variant-conflict (another\n120\t   baseline); or the authority's own :suspended and :closed answers.\n121\t   Nothing is stored unless the offer is admitted, and nothing is\n122\t   committed unless the store holds the body.\"\n123\t  [a store address bytes medium]\n124\t  (let [b (checkpoint/inspect address bytes)]\n125\t    (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n126\t      {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n127\t       :yin.k/inspection b}\n128\t      (let [decide (offer-decision address medium b)]\n129\t        (authority/locked\n130\t          a\n131\t          (fn []\n132\t            (let [p (authority/projection a)]\n133\t              (if (and p\n134\t                       (seq (::authority/facts (decide p)))\n135\t                       (not (store! store address bytes)))\n136\t                {:yin.k/status :suspended :yin.k/reason :content-unavailable}\n137\t                (authority/transition! a decide)))))))))\n138\t\n139\t\n140\t;; =============================================================================\n141\t;; The judge's writer: grants, lapses and refusals, each one transaction\n142\t;; =============================================================================\n143\t\n144\t(def ^:private ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n145\t\n146\t(def ^:private invalid {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value})\n147\t\n148\t\n149\t(def ^:private transport-error\n150\t  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n151\t\n152\t\n153\t(def ^:private grant-terms\n154\t  [:dao.lease/duration :dao.lease/proposal :dao.lease/max])\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- grant-decision\n158\t  \"Decide grant fact `g` of lease l on occurrence o to holder h.  The\n159\t   grant recorded for l is a replay only when its occurrence, holder and\n160\t   terms are g's.\"\n161\t  [g l o h]\n162\t  (fn [p]\n163\t    (let [known (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n164\t          recorded (get-in p [:leases l])]\n165\t      (cond\n166\t        (and recorded\n167\t             (= o (:yin.k/occurrence recorded))\n168\t             (= h (:dao.lease/holder recorded))\n169\t             (= (select-keys g grant-terms)\n170\t                (select-keys recorded grant-terms)))\n171\t        {::authority/reply ok}\n172\t        (or recorded\n173\t            (nil? known)\n174\t            (:yin.k/exhausted known)\n175\t            (:yin.k/quarantined known)\n176\t            (:yin.k/closed known)\n177\t            (some? (:dao.lease/lease known))\n178\t            (contains? (:answered p) [h (:dao.lease/proposal g)]))\n179\t        {::authority/reply invalid}\n180\t        :else\n181\t        {::authority/facts [g (custody/bound o l h (:yin.k/epoch known))]\n182\t         ::authority/reply ok}))))\n183\t\n184\t\n185\t(defn- lapse-decision\n186\t  \"Decide lapse fact `f` of lease l: the lapse and its occurrence's epoch\n187\t   change in one transaction, completing an eligible accepted report on\n188\t   release or policy reclaim. The lapse recorded for l with the same\n189\t   cause is a replay.\"\n190\t  [f l]\n191\t  (fn [p]\n192\t    (let [recorded (get-in p [:leases l])\n193\t          o (:yin.k/occurrence recorded)]\n194\t      (cond\n195\t        (and recorded\n196\t             (= (:dao.lease/cause f) (:dao.lease/cause recorded)))\n197\t        {::authority/reply ok}\n198\t        (or (nil? recorded)\n199\t            (contains? recorded :dao.lease/cause)\n200\t            (not= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease])))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"25311ae7-bba5-4028-86d0-afaa28ed48a3","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:16:34.868Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/grant.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant\n  \"Offers, grants and epoch bindings of M-next C slice C5, and the\n   reclaims, epochs and reopen of slice C6 (UCF 7.7.2, 7.7.7, 7.7.8;\n   docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md 14.2.2 and 14.2.3).\n\n   `offer!` admits one snapshot variant of an occurrence: it inspects\n   the bytes (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint), stores the accepted body in a\n   content store, and only then commits the offer fact with its\n   operation baseline, so the ledger never references missing content.\n   An uninspectable body commits nothing and stores nothing.  An offer\n   of a recorded variant is a replay; a known occurrence offered with\n   another origin, or a variant with another baseline, is refused.\n\n   The grant is the dao.lease judge's, composed per plan 1.3:\n   `judge-config` supplies the judge's `:writer`, a ledger adapter that\n   records an appended `:dao.lease/accepted` fact and its `:yin.k/bound`\n   binding as one transaction; its `:reclaim`, a readiness check that\n   revokes nothing; and its `:answer` hook, which grants one proposal per\n   offered, unheld occurrence and refuses the losing candidates.\n   `step!` runs a whole judge-step under the authority's lock, so the\n   hook and the writer see one projection.  The writer, not the hook,\n   enforces one live lease per occurrence.\n\n   The reclaim adapter contract (plan 1.3).  The judge marks a due lease\n   pending and calls `:reclaim`, which only reports readiness; the\n   revocation is the writer's lapse transaction, which holds the\n   `:dao.lease/lapsed` fact and its occurrence's epoch change\n   (`:yin.k/reclaimed`) together.  Nothing claiming the revocation\n   leaves the authority before that transaction commits: until then the\n   projection shows the lease live at its epoch.  A non-ok writer answer\n   leaves the lease pending in the judge and the projection unchanged,\n   and the ledger fold refuses a lapse without its epoch change.\n\n   `reopen!` is plan 1.5 steps 1 to 4 and 6: it opens the authority and\n   reclaims every tenure the ledger shows live, cause :policy, each as\n   one transaction, before it hands the authority out; nothing is\n   regranted.  `rebuild-judge` is step 5: the judge's `:seen` and\n   `:answered` from the ledger, its `:ledger` and `:queue` empty.\n\n   Slice C8 (yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion) hooks in three places: a\n   release lapse of a reported lease carries the closure and its edge,\n   a closed occurrence is never granted, and a successor's offer waits\n   for its predecessor's completion.\"\n  (:require [dao.lease :as lease]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion :as completion]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n\n\n(defn- reply\n  ([s] {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status s}})\n  ([s reason o]\n   {::authority/reply (cond-> {:yin.k/status s :yin.k/reason reason}\n                        (some? o) (assoc :yin.k/occurrence o))}))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Offers\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- offer-decision\n  \"Decide the offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` on `medium`\n   against projection p.\"\n  [address medium b]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence b)\n          known (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n          succession (when-not known (completion/offer-refusal p address b))]\n      (cond\n        (or (:yin.k/fork b)\n            (not (contains? #{:blocked :parked} (:yin.k/kind b))))\n        (reply :refused :not-offerable nil)\n        (not (custody/occurrence? o))\n        (reply :refused :malformed-occurrence nil)\n        (not= (:arbitration p)\n              (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n        (reply :refused :foreign-arbitration o)\n        (nil? medium) (reply :refused :missing-medium o)\n        (contains? (:yin.k/variants known) address)\n        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed :yin.k/occurrence o}}\n        (and known (not= (:yin.k/origin b)\n                         (get-in known [:yin.k/baseline :yin.k/origin])))\n        (reply :refused :occurrence-conflict o)\n        (and known (not= b (:yin.k/baseline known)))\n        (reply :refused :variant-conflict o)\n        succession (reply :refused succession o)\n        :else\n        {::authority/facts [(custody/offer o address medium b)]\n         ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed :yin.k/occurrence o}}))))\n\n\n(defn- store!\n  \"Put the body's bytes in the content store; true once it holds them.\"\n  [store address bytes]\n  (try\n    (contains? #{:inserted :present}\n               ((:put-bytes-fn store) address bytes))\n    (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) _\n      false)))\n\n\n(defn offer!\n  \"Admit the offer of the body whose canonical bytes are `bytes` at\n   segment address `address`, carried on `medium`.  `store` is a dao.jing\n   byte-store handle (`:put-bytes-fn`), where the accepted body is put\n   before the ledger references it.  Answers\n\n     {:yin.k/status :committed :yin.k/occurrence o :dao.space/t t}\n     {:yin.k/status :replayed :yin.k/occurrence o}   ; a recorded variant\n     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r ...}\n     {:yin.k/status :suspended :yin.k/reason :content-unavailable}\n\n   with r one of :uninspectable (carrying the inspector's refusal under\n   `:yin.k/inspection`), :not-offerable (a halted root), :malformed-\n   occurrence, :foreign-arbitration, :missing-medium,\n   :occurrence-conflict (another origin) and :variant-conflict (another\n   baseline); or the authority's own :suspended and :closed answers.\n   Nothing is stored unless the offer is admitted, and nothing is\n   committed unless the store holds the body.\"\n  [a store address bytes medium]\n  (let [b (checkpoint/inspect address bytes)]\n    (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n      {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n       :yin.k/inspection b}\n      (let [decide (offer-decision address medium b)]\n        (authority/locked\n          a\n          (fn []\n            (let [p (authority/projection a)]\n              (if (and p\n                       (seq (::authority/facts (decide p)))\n                       (not (store! store address bytes)))\n                {:yin.k/status :suspended :yin.k/reason :content-unavailable}\n                (authority/transition! a decide)))))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The judge's writer: grants, lapses and refusals, each one transaction\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def ^:private ok {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/ok})\n\n(def ^:private invalid {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/invalid-value})\n\n\n(def ^:private transport-error\n  {:dao.stream/outcome :dao.stream/transport-error})\n\n\n(def ^:private grant-terms\n  [:dao.lease/duration :dao.lease/proposal :dao.lease/max])\n\n\n(defn- grant-decision\n  \"Decide grant fact `g` of lease l on occurrence o to holder h.  The\n   grant recorded for l is a replay only when its occurrence, holder and\n   terms are g's.\"\n  [g l o h]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [known (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n          recorded (get-in p [:leases l])]\n      (cond\n        (and recorded\n             (= o (:yin.k/occurrence recorded))\n             (= h (:dao.lease/holder recorded))\n             (= (select-keys g grant-terms)\n                (select-keys recorded grant-terms)))\n        {::authority/reply ok}\n        (or recorded\n            (nil? known)\n            (:yin.k/exhausted known)\n            (:yin.k/quarantined known)\n            (:yin.k/closed known)\n            (some? (:dao.lease/lease known))\n            (contains? (:answered p) [h (:dao.lease/proposal g)]))\n        {::authority/reply invalid}\n        :else\n        {::authority/facts [g (custody/bound o l h (:yin.k/epoch known))]\n         ::authority/reply ok}))))\n\n\n(defn- lapse-decision\n  \"Decide lapse fact `f` of lease l: the lapse and its occurrence's epoch\n   change in one transaction, completing an eligible accepted report on\n   release or policy reclaim. The lapse recorded for l with the same\n   cause is a replay.\"\n  [f l]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [recorded (get-in p [:leases l])\n          o (:yin.k/occurrence recorded)]\n      (cond\n        (and recorded\n             (= (:dao.lease/cause f) (:dao.lease/cause recorded)))\n        {::authority/reply ok}\n        (or (nil? recorded)\n            (contains? recorded :dao.lease/cause)\n            (not= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease])))","numLines":200,"startLine":1,"totalLines":422}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Ba3cYADtDTP8in24tRtf8p","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfyz2daRKpwjAJuo8zyKo","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PSo2Lm4NPhMi7FCnHKufS3","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc","offset":1,"limit":235},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1789,"cache_read_input_tokens":176651,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1789},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"f9d7e222-ca81-4dad-8444-07085868eb7b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:16:35.987Z","request_id":"req_011Cfyz2dF6Dx5Gpzc5mADCY","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01PSo2Lm4NPhMi7FCnHKufS3":{"file_path":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc","offset":1,"limit":235}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PSo2Lm4NPhMi7FCnHKufS3","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion\n2\t  \"Completion of an occurrence, M-next C slice C8 (UCF 7.7.5 *Durable\n3\t   completion*, 7.7.6, 7.7.8 *Exhaustion*; docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n4\t   14.2.3 step 6).\n5\t\n6\t   The holder's exit is: append the successor to its carrier, report\n7\t   `:yin.k/resumed` naming the successor's address, then release.\n8\t   `report!` admits the report: the reporting author must be the\n9\t   lease's holder, the lease live, its occurrence not quarantined, and\n10\t   the successor's bytes must pass the inspector (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint:\n11\t   the address, version 1, the root role) with an origin naming this\n12\t   occurrence and lease.  A continuation must also name the same\n13\t   arbitration identity, be an occurrence the ledger has never seen, and\n14\t   carry a counter that continues the predecessor's (`:yin.k/next-op-seq`\n15\t   not below it).  A halted result carries none of those.  The authority\n16\t   records the report, with the successor occurrence it verified for a\n17\t   continuation; the bytes are not stored.\n18\t\n19\t   Completion is the grantor's transition, not the report.  When the\n20\t   judge's writer records a `:release` or `:policy` lapse of a reported lease\n21\t   (yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant), `closure` adds the closure and its one\n22\t   edge to that lapse's transaction, between the lapse and its epoch\n23\t   change, so no reader sees a closure without its edge or its lapse.\n24\t   The edge goes to the successor occurrence, or, for a halted result,\n25\t   is a terminal edge to the result's address.  A release or policy lapse with no\n26\t   report, a reclaim of any other cause, an exhausting reclaim (a lease\n27\t   bound at the epoch bound), a quarantined occurrence and a successor\n28\t   the ledger has meanwhile seen all leave a plain reclaim: the\n29\t   occurrence returns to offered, or stays exhausted or quarantined.  A\n30\t   closed occurrence never grants again.\n31\t\n32\t   The successors form one acyclic chain: one edge per predecessor, and\n33\t   one predecessor per successor, because an edge's successor is an\n34\t   occurrence the ledger has never seen; a result is no occurrence, so\n35\t   the chain ends there.  `offer-refusal` is the offer precondition for\n36\t   a body with an origin: it is admitted only as its predecessor's\n37\t   recorded successor in this ledger, at the reported address, after the\n38\t   closure.  Before closure it is `:awaiting-completion`; a body that can\n39\t   no longer become that successor, or whose predecessor this ledger\n40\t   never saw, is an `:orphan`, refused, so never offered and never\n41\t   grantable.\"\n42\t  (:require [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n43\t            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n44\t            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n46\t            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n47\t\n48\t\n49\t;; =============================================================================\n50\t;; Facts\n51\t;; =============================================================================\n52\t\n53\t(defn resumed\n54\t  \"The holder's report that occurrence `o`, under lease `l`, became the\n55\t   successor whose body is at segment address `address` (7.7.2).  The\n56\t   authority records it with `:yin.k/successor`, the occurrence it\n57\t   verified.\"\n58\t  [o l address]\n59\t  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/resumed\n60\t   :yin.k/occurrence o\n61\t   :dao.lease/lease l\n62\t   :yin.k/result address})\n63\t\n64\t\n65\t(defn completed\n66\t  \"The closure of occurrence `o` by release or policy reclaim of lease `l`.\"\n67\t  [o l]\n68\t  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/completed\n69\t   :yin.k/occurrence o\n70\t   :dao.lease/lease l})\n71\t\n72\t\n73\t(defn succeeded\n74\t  \"The edge from closed occurrence `o` to its successor `s`.\"\n75\t  [o s]\n76\t  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n77\t   :yin.k/occurrence o\n78\t   :yin.k/successor s})\n79\t\n80\t\n81\t(defn terminated\n82\t  \"The terminal edge from closed occurrence `o` to the address of its\n83\t   halted result.\"\n84\t  [o address]\n85\t  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n86\t   :yin.k/occurrence o\n87\t   :yin.k/result address})\n88\t\n89\t\n90\t;; =============================================================================\n91\t;; The report\n92\t;; =============================================================================\n93\t\n94\t(defn- successor-defect\n95\t  \"Why baseline `b` is not a successor of occurrence `o` under lease `l`\n96\t   against projection p, or nil.  A halted result is checked only for\n97\t   its origin: it carries no occurrence, arbitration or counter.\"\n98\t  [p o l b]\n99\t  (let [s (:yin.k/occurrence b)]\n100\t    (cond\n101\t      (not (and (= o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence]))\n102\t                (= l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease]))))\n103\t      :wrong-origin\n104\t      (= :halted (:yin.k/kind b)) nil\n105\t      (not= (:arbitration p)\n106\t            (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n107\t      :foreign-arbitration\n108\t      (ledger/successor-seen? p s) :seen-occurrence\n109\t      (neg? (cbor/num-compare\n110\t              (:yin.k/next-op-seq b)\n111\t              (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/baseline :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n112\t      :counter-regression\n113\t      :else nil)))\n114\t\n115\t\n116\t(defn- refused\n117\t  [reason]\n118\t  {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason reason}})\n119\t\n120\t\n121\t(defn- report-decision\n122\t  [author report b]\n123\t  (fn [p]\n124\t    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence report)\n125\t          l (:dao.lease/lease report)\n126\t          address (:yin.k/result report)\n127\t          entry (get-in p [:leases l])]\n128\t      (cond\n129\t        (nil? entry) (refused :unknown-lease)\n130\t        (not= o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)) (refused :wrong-occurrence)\n131\t        (not= author (:dao.lease/holder entry)) (refused :not-holder)\n132\t        (= address (:yin.k/result entry))\n133\t        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed}}\n134\t        (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause) (refused :ended-lease)\n135\t        (contains? entry :yin.k/result) (refused :report-conflict)\n136\t        (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]) (refused :quarantined)\n137\t        :else\n138\t        (if-let [d (successor-defect p o l b)]\n139\t          (refused d)\n140\t          {::authority/facts [(cond-> report\n141\t                                (not= :halted (:yin.k/kind b))\n142\t                                (assoc :yin.k/successor\n143\t                                       (:yin.k/occurrence b)))]\n144\t           ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed}})))))\n145\t\n146\t\n147\t(defn report!\n148\t  \"Admit holder `author`'s report `report` (a `resumed` fact) of the\n149\t   successor whose canonical bytes are `bytes`.  Answers\n150\t\n151\t     {:yin.k/status :committed :dao.space/t t}\n152\t     {:yin.k/status :replayed}                 ; the recorded report\n153\t     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r}\n154\t\n155\t   with r one of :malformed-report, :uninspectable (carrying the\n156\t   inspector's refusal under `:yin.k/inspection`), :unknown-lease,\n157\t   :wrong-occurrence, :not-holder, :ended-lease, :report-conflict\n158\t   (another report for the lease), :quarantined, :wrong-origin,\n159\t   :foreign-arbitration, :seen-occurrence and :counter-regression (the\n160\t   last three never for a halted result); or the authority's own\n161\t   :suspended and :closed answers.  A refused report writes nothing.\"\n162\t  [a author report bytes]\n163\t  (if-not (and (map? report)\n164\t               (= #{:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence :dao.lease/lease\n165\t                    :yin.k/result}\n166\t                  (set (keys report)))\n167\t               (= :yin.k/resumed (:yin.k/custody report))\n168\t               (custody/occurrence? (:yin.k/occurrence report))\n169\t               (some? (:dao.lease/lease report)))\n170\t    {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :malformed-report}\n171\t    (let [b (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/result report) bytes)]\n172\t      (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n173\t        {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n174\t         :yin.k/inspection b}\n175\t        (authority/transition! a (report-decision author report b))))))\n176\t\n177\t\n178\t;; =============================================================================\n179\t;; Completion, in the release or policy lapse's transaction\n180\t;; =============================================================================\n181\t\n182\t(defn closure\n183\t  \"The facts that complete the occurrence of lapse fact `f` against\n184\t   projection p: its closure and its one edge, when f is a `:release` or `:policy`\n185\t   lapse of a live, reported lease on an unquarantined occurrence whose\n186\t   reclaim does not exhaust it, and whose successor, if the report named\n187\t   a continuation, the ledger has not seen; else none.  The edge goes to\n188\t   the successor occurrence, or for a halted result is the terminal edge\n189\t   to its address.  They belong between the lapse and its epoch change.\"\n190\t  [p f]\n191\t  (let [l (:dao.lease/lease f)\n192\t        entry (get-in p [:leases l])\n193\t        o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)\n194\t        s (:yin.k/successor entry)]\n195\t    (if (and (contains? #{:release :policy} (:dao.lease/cause f))\n196\t             (contains? entry :yin.k/result)\n197\t             (not (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause))\n198\t             (= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease]))\n199\t             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed]))\n200\t             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]))\n201\t             (not= (:max-epoch p) (:yin.k/epoch entry))\n202\t             (not (and (some? s) (ledger/successor-seen? p s))))\n203\t      [(completed o l)\n204\t       (if (some? s) (succeeded o s) (terminated o (:yin.k/result entry)))]\n205\t      [])))\n206\t\n207\t\n208\t;; =============================================================================\n209\t;; Successor offers\n210\t;; =============================================================================\n211\t\n212\t(defn offer-refusal\n213\t  \"Why the first offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` may not be\n214\t   admitted against projection p, or nil.  A body with no origin, a\n215\t   first export, is unconstrained.  A body with an origin must be the\n216\t   successor its predecessor's closure recorded in this ledger, under\n217\t   the closing lease, at the reported address.  :awaiting-completion\n218\t   while the origin's lease is the live one; :orphan otherwise,\n219\t   including a predecessor this ledger never saw (7.7.8: a successor's\n220\t   arbitration is its predecessor's, unchanged).\"\n221\t  [p address b]\n222\t  (let [o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence])\n223\t        l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease])\n224\t        pred (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n225\t        closed (:yin.k/closed pred)]\n226\t    (cond\n227\t      (not (contains? b :yin.k/origin)) nil\n228\t      (nil? pred) :orphan\n229\t      (nil? closed)\n230\t      (if (= l (:dao.lease/lease pred)) :awaiting-completion :orphan)\n231\t      (and (= l (:dao.lease/lease closed))\n232\t           (= (:yin.k/occurrence b) (:yin.k/successor closed))\n233\t           (= address (get-in p [:leases l :yin.k/result])))\n234\t      nil\n235\t      :else :orphan)))"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"f4b826d5-d4f3-4d76-9b99-2a473ee87921","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:16:35.993Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/authority/completion.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.authority.completion\n  \"Completion of an occurrence, M-next C slice C8 (UCF 7.7.5 *Durable\n   completion*, 7.7.6, 7.7.8 *Exhaustion*; docs/design/yin.vm.linker.dht.md\n   14.2.3 step 6).\n\n   The holder's exit is: append the successor to its carrier, report\n   `:yin.k/resumed` naming the successor's address, then release.\n   `report!` admits the report: the reporting author must be the\n   lease's holder, the lease live, its occurrence not quarantined, and\n   the successor's bytes must pass the inspector (yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint:\n   the address, version 1, the root role) with an origin naming this\n   occurrence and lease.  A continuation must also name the same\n   arbitration identity, be an occurrence the ledger has never seen, and\n   carry a counter that continues the predecessor's (`:yin.k/next-op-seq`\n   not below it).  A halted result carries none of those.  The authority\n   records the report, with the successor occurrence it verified for a\n   continuation; the bytes are not stored.\n\n   Completion is the grantor's transition, not the report.  When the\n   judge's writer records a `:release` or `:policy` lapse of a reported lease\n   (yin.vm.ucf.authority.grant), `closure` adds the closure and its one\n   edge to that lapse's transaction, between the lapse and its epoch\n   change, so no reader sees a closure without its edge or its lapse.\n   The edge goes to the successor occurrence, or, for a halted result,\n   is a terminal edge to the result's address.  A release or policy lapse with no\n   report, a reclaim of any other cause, an exhausting reclaim (a lease\n   bound at the epoch bound), a quarantined occurrence and a successor\n   the ledger has meanwhile seen all leave a plain reclaim: the\n   occurrence returns to offered, or stays exhausted or quarantined.  A\n   closed occurrence never grants again.\n\n   The successors form one acyclic chain: one edge per predecessor, and\n   one predecessor per successor, because an edge's successor is an\n   occurrence the ledger has never seen; a result is no occurrence, so\n   the chain ends there.  `offer-refusal` is the offer precondition for\n   a body with an origin: it is admitted only as its predecessor's\n   recorded successor in this ledger, at the reported address, after the\n   closure.  Before closure it is `:awaiting-completion`; a body that can\n   no longer become that successor, or whose predecessor this ledger\n   never saw, is an `:orphan`, refused, so never offered and never\n   grantable.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.authority :as authority]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.checkpoint :as checkpoint]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.custody :as custody]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.ledger :as ledger]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Facts\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn resumed\n  \"The holder's report that occurrence `o`, under lease `l`, became the\n   successor whose body is at segment address `address` (7.7.2).  The\n   authority records it with `:yin.k/successor`, the occurrence it\n   verified.\"\n  [o l address]\n  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/resumed\n   :yin.k/occurrence o\n   :dao.lease/lease l\n   :yin.k/result address})\n\n\n(defn completed\n  \"The closure of occurrence `o` by release or policy reclaim of lease `l`.\"\n  [o l]\n  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/completed\n   :yin.k/occurrence o\n   :dao.lease/lease l})\n\n\n(defn succeeded\n  \"The edge from closed occurrence `o` to its successor `s`.\"\n  [o s]\n  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n   :yin.k/occurrence o\n   :yin.k/successor s})\n\n\n(defn terminated\n  \"The terminal edge from closed occurrence `o` to the address of its\n   halted result.\"\n  [o address]\n  {:yin.k/custody :yin.k/succeeded\n   :yin.k/occurrence o\n   :yin.k/result address})\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The report\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn- successor-defect\n  \"Why baseline `b` is not a successor of occurrence `o` under lease `l`\n   against projection p, or nil.  A halted result is checked only for\n   its origin: it carries no occurrence, arbitration or counter.\"\n  [p o l b]\n  (let [s (:yin.k/occurrence b)]\n    (cond\n      (not (and (= o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence]))\n                (= l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease]))))\n      :wrong-origin\n      (= :halted (:yin.k/kind b)) nil\n      (not= (:arbitration p)\n            (get-in b [:yin.k/arbitration :dao.stream/identity]))\n      :foreign-arbitration\n      (ledger/successor-seen? p s) :seen-occurrence\n      (neg? (cbor/num-compare\n              (:yin.k/next-op-seq b)\n              (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/baseline :yin.k/next-op-seq])))\n      :counter-regression\n      :else nil)))\n\n\n(defn- refused\n  [reason]\n  {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason reason}})\n\n\n(defn- report-decision\n  [author report b]\n  (fn [p]\n    (let [o (:yin.k/occurrence report)\n          l (:dao.lease/lease report)\n          address (:yin.k/result report)\n          entry (get-in p [:leases l])]\n      (cond\n        (nil? entry) (refused :unknown-lease)\n        (not= o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)) (refused :wrong-occurrence)\n        (not= author (:dao.lease/holder entry)) (refused :not-holder)\n        (= address (:yin.k/result entry))\n        {::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :replayed}}\n        (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause) (refused :ended-lease)\n        (contains? entry :yin.k/result) (refused :report-conflict)\n        (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]) (refused :quarantined)\n        :else\n        (if-let [d (successor-defect p o l b)]\n          (refused d)\n          {::authority/facts [(cond-> report\n                                (not= :halted (:yin.k/kind b))\n                                (assoc :yin.k/successor\n                                       (:yin.k/occurrence b)))]\n           ::authority/reply {:yin.k/status :committed}})))))\n\n\n(defn report!\n  \"Admit holder `author`'s report `report` (a `resumed` fact) of the\n   successor whose canonical bytes are `bytes`.  Answers\n\n     {:yin.k/status :committed :dao.space/t t}\n     {:yin.k/status :replayed}                 ; the recorded report\n     {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason r}\n\n   with r one of :malformed-report, :uninspectable (carrying the\n   inspector's refusal under `:yin.k/inspection`), :unknown-lease,\n   :wrong-occurrence, :not-holder, :ended-lease, :report-conflict\n   (another report for the lease), :quarantined, :wrong-origin,\n   :foreign-arbitration, :seen-occurrence and :counter-regression (the\n   last three never for a halted result); or the authority's own\n   :suspended and :closed answers.  A refused report writes nothing.\"\n  [a author report bytes]\n  (if-not (and (map? report)\n               (= #{:yin.k/custody :yin.k/occurrence :dao.lease/lease\n                    :yin.k/result}\n                  (set (keys report)))\n               (= :yin.k/resumed (:yin.k/custody report))\n               (custody/occurrence? (:yin.k/occurrence report))\n               (some? (:dao.lease/lease report)))\n    {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :malformed-report}\n    (let [b (checkpoint/inspect (:yin.k/result report) bytes)]\n      (if (contains? b :yin.k/status)\n        {:yin.k/status :refused :yin.k/reason :uninspectable\n         :yin.k/inspection b}\n        (authority/transition! a (report-decision author report b))))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Completion, in the release or policy lapse's transaction\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn closure\n  \"The facts that complete the occurrence of lapse fact `f` against\n   projection p: its closure and its one edge, when f is a `:release` or `:policy`\n   lapse of a live, reported lease on an unquarantined occurrence whose\n   reclaim does not exhaust it, and whose successor, if the report named\n   a continuation, the ledger has not seen; else none.  The edge goes to\n   the successor occurrence, or for a halted result is the terminal edge\n   to its address.  They belong between the lapse and its epoch change.\"\n  [p f]\n  (let [l (:dao.lease/lease f)\n        entry (get-in p [:leases l])\n        o (:yin.k/occurrence entry)\n        s (:yin.k/successor entry)]\n    (if (and (contains? #{:release :policy} (:dao.lease/cause f))\n             (contains? entry :yin.k/result)\n             (not (contains? entry :dao.lease/cause))\n             (= l (get-in p [:occurrences o :dao.lease/lease]))\n             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/closed]))\n             (not (get-in p [:occurrences o :yin.k/quarantined]))\n             (not= (:max-epoch p) (:yin.k/epoch entry))\n             (not (and (some? s) (ledger/successor-seen? p s))))\n      [(completed o l)\n       (if (some? s) (succeeded o s) (terminated o (:yin.k/result entry)))]\n      [])))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Successor offers\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn offer-refusal\n  \"Why the first offer of variant `address` with baseline `b` may not be\n   admitted against projection p, or nil.  A body with no origin, a\n   first export, is unconstrained.  A body with an origin must be the\n   successor its predecessor's closure recorded in this ledger, under\n   the closing lease, at the reported address.  :awaiting-completion\n   while the origin's lease is the live one; :orphan otherwise,\n   including a predecessor this ledger never saw (7.7.8: a successor's\n   arbitration is its predecessor's, unchanged).\"\n  [p address b]\n  (let [o (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :yin.k/occurrence])\n        l (get-in b [:yin.k/origin :dao.lease/lease])\n        pred (get-in p [:occurrences o])\n        closed (:yin.k/closed pred)]\n    (cond\n      (not (contains? b :yin.k/origin)) nil\n      (nil? pred) :orphan\n      (nil? closed)\n      (if (= l (:dao.lease/lease pred)) :awaiting-completion :orphan)\n      (and (= l (:dao.lease/lease closed))\n           (= (:yin.k/occurrence b) (:yin.k/successor closed))\n           (= address (get-in p [:leases l :yin.k/result])))\n      nil\n      :else :orphan)))","numLines":235,"startLine":1,"totalLines":236}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PSo2Lm4NPhMi7FCnHKufS3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
