{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01EuW3qKkJPcot4bGt9dE8PV","type":"tool_result","content":"100\t(defn- refuse!\n101\t  [status data]\n102\t  (throw (ex-info (str \"Handoff refused: \" (name status))\n103\t                  (merge {:yin.k/status status} data))))\n104\t\n105\t\n106\t(defn- non-portable!\n107\t  [kind data]\n108\t  (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable (assoc data :yin.k/kind kind)))\n109\t\n110\t\n111\t(defn- unsatisfied!\n112\t  ([] (unsatisfied! nil))\n113\t  ([identity]\n114\t   (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n115\t            (cond-> {} (some? identity)\n116\t                    (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity)))))\n117\t\n118\t\n119\t(defn- undecodable!\n120\t  [data]\n121\t  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable data))\n122\t\n123\t\n124\t(defn- not-at-safepoint!\n125\t  [pc]\n126\t  (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint {:yin.k/pc pc}))\n127\t\n128\t\n129\t(defn- outcome\n130\t  \"The S7.9 data outcome exception `e` carries, or nil.\"\n131\t  [e]\n132\t  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n133\t    (when (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d)))\n134\t\n135\t\n136\t(defn- call!\n137\t  \"Run `f`, answering its value, or the data outcome it refused with.\n138\t   A throw with no outcome vocabulary is a defect, not a refusal: it\n139\t   propagates.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"27c19100-d5b3-4a0b-8779-96daaa48ff05","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:19:20.182Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/src/cljc/yin/vm/ucf/handoff.cljc","content":"(defn- refuse!\n  [status data]\n  (throw (ex-info (str \"Handoff refused: \" (name status))\n                  (merge {:yin.k/status status} data))))\n\n\n(defn- non-portable!\n  [kind data]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/non-portable (assoc data :yin.k/kind kind)))\n\n\n(defn- unsatisfied!\n  ([] (unsatisfied! nil))\n  ([identity]\n   (refuse! :yin.k/unsatisfied\n            (cond-> {} (some? identity)\n                    (assoc :dao.stream/identity identity)))))\n\n\n(defn- undecodable!\n  [data]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/undecodable data))\n\n\n(defn- not-at-safepoint!\n  [pc]\n  (refuse! :yin.k/not-at-safepoint {:yin.k/pc pc}))\n\n\n(defn- outcome\n  \"The S7.9 data outcome exception `e` carries, or nil.\"\n  [e]\n  (let [d (ex-data e)]\n    (when (and (map? d) (contains? d :yin.k/status)) d)))\n\n\n(defn- call!\n  \"Run `f`, answering its value, or the data outcome it refused with.\n   A throw with no outcome vocabulary is a defect, not a refusal: it\n   propagates.\"","numLines":40,"startLine":100,"totalLines":3784}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01EuW3qKkJPcot4bGt9dE8PV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
