{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q26ifW9AkMm6uZJn2UZ7wQ","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n2\t  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n3\t   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n4\t\n5\t   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n6\t   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n7\t   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n8\t   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n9\t   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n10\t   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n11\t   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n12\t   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n13\t   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n14\t\n15\t   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n16\t   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n17\t   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n18\t   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n19\t   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n20\t   layout refusals close the file.\"\n21\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n22\t            [dao.jing :as jing]\n23\t            [dao.stream :as stream]\n24\t            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n25\t            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n26\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n27\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n28\t            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n29\t            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n30\t            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n31\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n32\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n33\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n34\t            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n35\t            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n36\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n37\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n38\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n39\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n40\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n41\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n42\t            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n43\t            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n44\t            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n45\t            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t;; =============================================================================\n49\t;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n50\t;; =============================================================================\n51\t\n52\t(def source-index\n53\t  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n54\t   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n55\t  (atom {}))\n56\t\n57\t\n58\t(def code-index\n59\t  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n60\t  (atom {}))\n61\t\n62\t\n63\t(def ^:dynamic *projected*\n64\t  \"When bound, an atom {A v} of the vectors one world projected: the\n65\t   layouts' spaces read it instead of the whole file's code-index, so an\n66\t   alpha-equivalent A an unrelated fixture projected widens no lookup.\"\n67\t  nil)\n68\t\n69\t\n70\t(defn project\n71\t  [ast]\n72\t  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n73\t        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n74\t    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n75\t    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n76\t    (when *projected* (swap! *projected* assoc a v))\n77\t    v))\n78\t\n79\t\n80\t(defn scoped\n81\t  \"f's result, every vector it projects recorded in a fresh *projected*.\"\n82\t  [f]\n83\t  (binding [*projected* (atom {})] (f)))\n84\t\n85\t\n86\t(defn file-wide\n87\t  \"f's result, the layouts' spaces reading every vector the file ever\n88\t   projected: only the fixtures that show that contamination.\"\n89\t  [f]\n90\t  (binding [*projected* code-index] (f)))\n91\t\n92\t\n93\t(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n94\t\n95\t\n96\t(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n97\t  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n98\t   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n99\t   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n100\t  :semantic-register)\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n104\t\n105\t\n106\t(defn- composition\n107\t  [opts]\n108\t  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n109\t          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n110\t          :modules stream-modules}\n111\t         opts))\n112\t\n113\t\n114\t(defn- kernel-opts\n115\t  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n116\t   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n117\t  [opts]\n118\t  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n119\t    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n120\t\n121\t\n122\t(defn machine\n123\t  ([] (machine {}))\n124\t  ([opts]\n125\t   (case *lane*\n126\t     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n127\t     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n128\t     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n129\t\n130\t\n131\t(defn lane-of\n132\t  [m]\n133\t  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n134\t    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n135\t          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n136\t          :else :semantic-register)))\n137\t\n138\t\n139\t(def segment-of\n140\t  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n141\t  (memoize layout/segment))\n142\t\n143\t\n144\t(defn kernel-space\n145\t  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k\n146\t   holds, among those this world projected (`scoped`), or the file ever\n147\t   projected (`file-wide`). Unbound, it throws: an independent world's\n148\t   lookups never read another fixture's vectors.\"\n149\t  [k]\n150\t  (when-not *projected*\n151\t    (throw (ex-info \"kernel-space outside scoped or file-wide\" {})))\n152\t  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n153\t        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n154\t    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @*projected*))))))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn- kernel-load\n158\t  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n159\t   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n160\t  [k v]\n161\t  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n162\t        sg (segment-of v)\n163\t        k (if (= :stack kind)\n164\t            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n165\t            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n166\t        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n167\t                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n168\t    (if (= :stack kind)\n169\t      (assoc k :stack [])\n170\t      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n171\t\n172\t\n173\t(defn load-program\n174\t  [m ast]\n175\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n176\t    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n177\t    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n178\t\n179\t\n180\t(defn lane-closure\n181\t  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n182\t  [m c]\n183\t  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n184\t    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n185\t    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n186\t\n187\t\n188\t(defn lift-opts\n189\t  []\n190\t  {:source-index @source-index})\n191\t\n192\t\n193\t(defn error\n194\t  [f]\n195\t  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n196\t\n197\t\n198\t;; =============================================================================\n199\t;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n200\t;; =============================================================================\n201\t\n202\t(defn cat-of\n203\t  [p q]\n204\t  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n205\t\n206\t\n207\t(defn with-cat\n208\t  [ast]\n209\t  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n210\t\n211\t\n212\t(defn nest\n213\t  [d op]\n214\t  (if (zero? d) op (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n215\t\n216\t\n217\t(def segments\n218\t  \"[label wrap expected-of-bare-result] (§5.2).\"\n219\t  [[:bare identity identity]\n220\t   [:operand #(cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) %) (fn [r] [:operand r])]\n221\t   [:depth-3 #(nest 3 %) (fn [r] [3 [2 [1 r]]])]\n222\t   [:captured #(s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n223\t                       (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y)) %))\n224\t                               (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg))))\n225\t    (fn [r] [:captured :arg r])]])\n226\t\n227\t\n228\t(defn with-stream\n229\t  [body]\n230\t  (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's)) body)))\n231\t\n232\t\n233\t(defn tail\n234\t  [ast]\n235\t  (assoc ast :tail? true))\n236\t\n237\t\n238\t(defn normalize\n239\t  [x]\n240\t  (cond\n241\t    (values/continuation? x) :continuation\n242\t    (values/closure? x) :closure\n243\t    (vector? x) (mapv normalize x)\n244\t    (seq? x) (apply list (map normalize x))\n245\t    (set? x) (into #{} (map normalize) x)\n246\t    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(normalize k) (normalize v)])) x)\n247\t    :else x))\n248\t\n249\t\n250\t;; =============================================================================\n251\t;; The rows of §5.2: one builder each, answering the parked machine\n252\t;; =============================================================================\n253\t;;\n254\t;; A world: :machine, :kind, :reason (blocked rows), :steps (each followed by\n255\t;; a drive) or :resume, :finish (records the effect trace), :trace, and\n256\t;; :receiver (fresh opts and a finish for the receiver's own composition).\n257\t\n258\t(defn reader\n259\t  \"A reader parked on (next-of c); :pre values are appended and the\n260\t   machine re-run first.\"\n261\t  ([wrap op] (reader wrap op [] \"B\" {}))\n262\t  ([wrap op pre value opts]\n263\t   (let [m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine opts) (with-stream (with-cat (wrap op)))))\n264\t         src (s/stream-of m0)\n265\t         m (reduce (fn [m x] (stream/append! src x) (vm/run m)) m0 pre)]\n266\t     {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src value)] :trace (atom [])})))\n267\t\n268\t\n269\t(defn writer\n270\t  [wrap]\n271\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n272\t        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n273\t        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n274\t        m0 (load-program (machine) (with-cat (wrap {:type :stream/put :target (s/v 'w) :val (s/lit \"v\")})))\n275\t        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n276\t        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n277\t    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})) :kind :blocked :reason :put :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n278\t     :steps [take!] :finish take! :trace trace}))\n279\t\n280\t\n281\t(defn own-call-pair\n282\t  [trace]\n283\t  (let [own-in (s/ring 8) own-out (s/ring 8)]\n284\t    {:opts {:call-in own-in :call-out own-out :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n285\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n286\t\n287\t\n288\t(defn caller\n289\t  [wrap call-in call-out]\n290\t  (vm/run (load-program (machine {:call-in call-in :call-out call-out\n291\t                                  :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest call-out :test)})\n292\t                        (with-cat (wrap (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))))\n293\t\n294\t\n295\t(defn sent-ffi\n296\t  [wrap]\n297\t  (let [trace (atom []) call-in (s/ring 8) call-out (s/ring 8)\n298\t        m (caller wrap call-in call-out)\n299\t        id (ffi/response-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n300\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :ffi :call-id id\n301\t     :steps [#(stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\"))]\n302\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain call-in))\n303\t     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace) :trace trace}))\n304\t\n305\t\n306\t(defn retained-ffi\n307\t  [wrap]\n308\t  (let [trace (atom []) call-in (support/one-slot-stream \"call-in\") call-out (s/ring 8)\n309\t        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n310\t        m (caller wrap call-in call-out)\n311\t        id (ffi/request-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n312\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :ffi-request :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n313\t     :steps [#(stream/next call-in 0)\n314\t             (fn []\n315\t               (swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next call-in 0)))\n316\t               (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\")))]\n317\t     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace) :trace trace}))\n318\t\n319\t\n320\t(defn module-response\n321\t  [body exports]\n322\t  {:status :ok :image {:value (project body)}\n323\t   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports exports} :obligations []})\n324\t\n325\t\n326\t(def plain-body (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42))))\n327\t\n328\t\n329\t(def blocking-body\n330\t  \"host.mod's body reads a stream nothing feeds yet, then defines f. No\n331\t   binding holds the stream, so f's E does not capture it.\"\n332\t  (s/then (s/next-of (s/cursor-of {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})) (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42)))))\n333\t\n334\t\n335\t(defn require-op\n336\t  [tail?]\n337\t  (let [call (s/app (s/v 'require) (s/lit 'host.mod))]\n338\t    (if tail? (s/app (s/lam ['u] (tail call)) (s/lit 0)) call)))\n339\t\n340\t\n341\t(defn link-receiver\n342\t  [trace]\n343\t  (fn []\n344\t    (let [rq (s/ring 64)]\n345\t      {:opts {:link-request rq :link-response (s/ring 64)} :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain rq))})))\n346\t\n347\t\n348\t(defn linking\n349\t  \"A require parked in :link-response (or :link-request behind a full,\n350\t   warmed request stream when retained?).\"\n351\t  [wrap tail? retained?]\n352\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n353\t        request (if retained? (support/one-slot-stream \"link-request\") (s/ring 64))\n354\t        response (s/ring 64)\n355\t        _ (when retained? (stream/append! request :warmed))\n356\t        m (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n357\t                                (with-cat (wrap (require-op tail?)))))\n358\t        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m)))\n359\t        answer! #(stream/append! response (assoc (module-response plain-body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))]\n360\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason (if retained? :link-request :link-response)\n361\t     :surfaces #{:reader :writer} :trace trace\n362\t     :steps (if retained? [#(stream/next request 0) answer!] [answer!])\n363\t     :finish (if retained?\n364\t               #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next request 0)))\n365\t               #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request)))\n366\t     :receiver (link-receiver trace)}))\n367\t\n368\t\n369\t(defn installing\n370\t  \"A require parked on :install beside its blocked child.\"\n371\t  [wrap tail? phase]\n372\t  (let [trace (atom [])\n373\t        request (s/ring 64) response (s/ring 64)\n374\t        m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n375\t                                 (with-cat (wrap (require-op tail?)))))\n376\t        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m0)))\n377\t        _ (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response blocking-body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))\n378\t        m1 (vm/run m0)\n379\t        m (if phase (assoc-in m1 [:installs 'host.mod :phase] phase) m1)\n380\t        child (get-in m [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\n381\t        child-stream (s/stream-of child)]\n382\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :install :trace trace\n383\t     :steps [#(stream/append! child-stream :fed)]\n384\t     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request))\n385\t     :receiver (link-receiver trace)}))\n386\t\n387\t\n388\t(defn module-context\n389\t  \"Blocked inside host.mod's exported closure, whose E names store-of host.mod.\"\n390\t  [wrap]\n391\t  (let [request (s/ring 64) response (s/ring 64)\n392\t        body (s/def! 'f (s/lam ['c] (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c))))\n393\t        m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n394\t                                 (with-stream (with-cat (wrap (s/then (s/app (s/v 'require) (s/lit 'host.mod))\n395\t                                                                      (s/app (s/v 'host.mod/f) (s/v 'c))))))))\n396\t        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m0)))\n397\t        _ (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))\n398\t        m (vm/run m0)\n399\t        src (s/stream-of m)]\n400\t    ;; The carrier holds module stores, not registry entries: the receiver's\n401\t    ;; composition links host.mod itself, so its relift discharges host.mod/f.\n402\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")] :trace (atom [])\n403\t     :receiver (constantly {:opts {:modules (:modules m)}})}))\n404\t\n405\t\n406\t(defn run-beside\n407\t  [m ast]\n408\t  (vm/run (load-program m ast)))\n409\t\n410\t\n411\t(defn parking\n412\t  [m]\n413\t  (let [pid (:id (vm/value m))]\n414\t    {:machine m :kind :parked :pid pid :trace (atom [])\n415\t     :resume #(run-beside % {:type :vm/resume :parked-id pid :val (s/lit \"back\")})}))\n416\t\n417\t\n418\t(defn module-store-cursors\n419\t  \"An explicit park whose module store holds two cursor references nothing\n420\t   else reaches, named by a module closure in the task store.\"\n421\t  [wrap]\n422\t  (let [ring (s/ring 4)\n423\t        ast (with-cat (wrap (s/app (s/lam ['p] {:type :vm/park}) (s/lit 1))))\n424\t        v (project ast)\n425\t        m (vm/run (load-program (machine) ast))\n426\t        cursor (fn [m]\n427\t                 (let [[ref m] (engine/attach-resource m ring) [id m] (engine/gensym m \"cursor\")]\n428\t                   (engine/handle-cursor m {:stream ref} id)))\n429\t        [c1 m] (cursor m)\n430\t        [c2 m] (cursor m)\n431\t        closure (first (filter #(= :closure (first %)) v))\n432\t        clo (lane-closure m {:type :closure :params (nth closure 2) :entry (nth closure 3)\n433\t                             :segment (jing/segment-key v) :env {engine/store-of-key 'host.mod}})]\n434\t    (parking (assoc m :store {'mod clo} :module-stores {'host.mod {'c c1 'd c2}}))))\n435\t\n436\t\n437\t(defn free-env-world\n438\t  [wrap env]\n439\t  (reader wrap (s/let1 'f (s/lam [] (s/v 'x)) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))) (s/lit 1)))\n440\t          [] \"B\" {:env env}))\n441\t\n442\t\n443\t(def read-op (s/next-of (s/v 'c)))\n444\t\n445\t\n446\t(def capture {:type :vm/current-continuation})\n447\t\n448\t\n449\t(def rows\n450\t  \"[row bare-result build]: rows 1-19, 21, 22, 24 of §5.2. A nil result\n451\t   compares with the reference only.\"\n452\t  [[1 [\"A\" \"B\"] #(reader % (s/let1 'a read-op (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'a)) read-op)) [\"A\"] \"B\" {})]\n453\t   [2 nil writer]\n454\t   [3 \"echo!\" sent-ffi]\n455\t   [4 \"echo!\" retained-ffi]\n456\t   [5 [:ordinary \"B\"] #(reader % (cat-of (s/lit [:ordinary]) (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c))))]\n457\t   [6 \"B\" #(reader % (s/app (s/lam ['u] (tail (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c)))) (s/lit 0)))]\n458\t   [7 'host.mod #(linking % false true)]\n459\t   [8 'host.mod #(linking % false false)]\n460\t   [9 'host.mod #(linking % true false)]\n461\t   [10 'host.mod #(installing % false nil)]\n462\t   [11 'host.mod #(installing % false :running)]\n463\t   [12 'host.mod #(installing % true nil)]\n464\t   [13 \"back\" #(parking (vm/run (load-program (machine) (with-cat (% {:type :vm/park})))))]\n465\t   [14 [:continuation \"B\"] #(reader % (s/let1 'k capture (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) read-op)))]\n466\t   [15 :done #(reader % (s/let1 'k capture {:type :if :test (s/app (s/v '=) (s/v 'k) (s/lit :second))\n467\t                                            :consequent (s/lit :done)\n468\t                                            :alternate (s/let1 'r read-op (s/app (s/v 'k) (s/lit :second)))})\n469\t                      [] \"x\" {})]\n470\t   [16 [:continuation :continuation \"B\"]\n471\t    #(reader % (s/let1 'k1 capture (s/let1 'k2 capture (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k1)) (s/v 'k2)) read-op))))]\n472\t   [17 \"B\" module-context]\n473\t   [18 \"back\" module-store-cursors]\n474\t   [19 42 #(let [m (vm/run (load-program (machine) (with-cat (% (s/lit 42)))))]\n475\t             {:machine m :kind :halted :trace (atom [])})]\n476\t   [21 99 #(free-env-world % {'x 99})]\n477\t   [22 [nil \"B\"] #(reader % (s/let1 'pair (s/lam ['p 'q] (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'p)) (s/v 'q)))\n478\t                                    (s/app (s/v 'pair) (s/lit nil) read-op)))]\n479\t   [24 \"echo!\" sent-ffi]])\n480\t\n481\t\n482\t(defn tail-effect-halt\n483\t  \"Row 20, outside the wrappers: a setup batch to halt, then the root tail\n484\t   call (stream/next! c) with an empty K.\"\n485\t  []\n486\t  (let [setup (vm/run (load-program (machine) (s/then (s/def! 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})\n487\t                                                      (s/def! 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's))))))\n488\t        m (run-beside setup (tail (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c))))\n489\t        src (s/stream-of m)]\n490\t    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src \"B\")] :trace (atom [])}))\n491\t\n492\t\n493\t;; =============================================================================\n494\t;; The two runs\n495\t;; =============================================================================\n496\t\n497\t(defn drive-local\n498\t  [m]\n499\t  (loop [m (vm/run m) n 12]\n500\t    (if (or (not (vm/blocked? m)) (zero? n)) m (recur (vm/run m) (dec n)))))\n501\t\n502\t\n503\t(defn drive-peers\n504\t  [m peers]\n505\t  (loop [m (vm/run m) n 12]\n506\t    (if (or (not (vm/blocked? m)) (zero? n))\n507\t      m\n508\t      (do (run! s/serve-mirror! peers) (recur (vm/run m) (dec n))))))\n509\t\n510\t\n511\t(defn satisfy\n512\t  [world m drive]\n513\t  (if-let [resume (:resume world)]\n514\t    (resume m)\n515\t    (reduce (fn [m step] (step) (drive m)) m (:steps world))))\n516\t\n517\t\n518\t(defn reference\n519\t  [world]\n520\t  (let [done (satisfy world (:machine world) drive-local)]\n521\t    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n522\t    {:halted (vm/halted? done) :value (normalize (vm/value done)) :trace @(:trace world)}))\n523\t\n524\t\n525\t(defn served\n526\t  \"A served table over a fresh toy: [serve! correspondence-fn].\"\n527\t  [surfaces]\n528\t  (let [t (s/toy) peer (s/served-peer t)]\n529\t    {:toy t :peer peer :serve! (s/server peer (:channel t) surfaces)}))\n530\t\n531\t\n532\t(defn recording-attacher\n533\t  \"The receiver's attach!, counting attaches and recording each\n534\t   reflection's source identity.\"\n535\t  [t]\n536\t  (let [base (s/attacher t) origin (atom {}) n (atom 0)]\n537\t    {:attach! (fn [d]\n538\t                (swap! n inc)\n539\t                (let [r (base d)]\n540\t                  (when-let [h (:dao.stream/handle r)] (swap! origin assoc h (:dao.stream/identity d)))\n541\t                  r))\n542\t     :origin origin :count n}))\n543\t\n544\t\n545\t(defn handed-off\n546\t  \"Lift, lower into a fresh receiver, relift at once, then satisfy through\n547\t   the source's streams.\"\n548\t  [world]\n549\t  (let [surfaces (or (:surfaces world) #{:reader})\n550\t        {:keys [toy peer serve!]} (served surfaces)\n551\t        wire (rows/lift-task (:machine world) serve! (lift-opts))\n552\t        corr (into {} (map (fn [[id _]] [id id])) @(:table peer))\n553\t        receiver ((or (:receiver world) (constantly nil)))\n554\t        {:keys [attach! origin] n :count} (recording-attacher toy)\n555\t        recv (rows/lower-task (machine (merge {:attach-stream attach!} (:opts receiver))) wire attach!)\n556\t        attaches @n\n557\t        again (served surfaces)\n558\t        relift (rows/lift-task recv (:serve! again) (lift-opts))\n559\t        corr2 (into {} (map (fn [[id e]] [id (get @origin (:handle e))])) @(:table (:peer again)))\n560\t        done (satisfy world recv #(drive-peers % [peer]))\n561\t        _ (s/serve-mirror! peer)]\n562\t    (when-let [f (:finish world)] (f))\n563\t    (when-let [f (:finish receiver)] (f))\n564\t    {:wire wire :recv recv :relift relift :corr corr :corr2 corr2 :attaches attaches\n565\t     :halted (vm/halted? done) :value (normalize (vm/value done)) :trace @(:trace world)}))\n566\t\n567\t\n568\t(defn root-task\n569\t  [wire]\n570\t  (rows/decode wire))\n571\t\n572\t\n573\t(defn stream-identities\n574\t  \"The distinct stream identities of the whole carrier, install children\n575\t   included: one row table serves the tree.\"\n576\t  [wire]\n577\t  (into #{} (keep (fn [r] (when (= :stream (second r)) (nth r 2)))) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n578\t\n579\t\n580\t(defn rows-in\n581\t  \"Every row node the decoded tree x reaches, once per path.\"\n582\t  [x]\n583\t  (cond\n584\t    (and (map? x) (contains? x :kind) (contains? x :slots)) (cons x (rows-in (:slots x)))\n585\t    (sequential? x) (mapcat rows-in x)\n586\t    :else nil))\n587\t\n588\t\n589\t(defn stream-occurrences\n590\t  \"How many times the decoded tree reaches a :stream row.\"\n591\t  [x]\n592\t  (count (filter #(= :stream (:kind %)) (rows-in x))))\n593\t\n594\t\n595\t(defn slot\n596\t  [task i]\n597\t  (nth (:slots task) i))\n598\t\n599\t\n600\t(defn first-pending"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"7f11f7bf-e44d-4768-ac1b-fbb10ddee107","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:20:04.016Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-srvm-p7a/test/yin/vm/semantic_register/safepoint_harness_test.cljc","content":"(ns yin.vm.semantic-register.safepoint-harness-test\n  \"Phase 6b: the safepoint harness on the :semantic-register lane\n   (docs/design/yin.vm.semantic-register-vm.continuation.md §5, §8.2).\n\n   Each row of the §5.2 matrix is built twice under each of the four\n   segment wrappers: the reference build is satisfied and run on its own\n   machine; the handoff build is lifted with rows/lift-task, lowered with\n   rows/lower-task into a fresh receiver over the toy channel, relifted at\n   once, then satisfied through the source's streams. Result and effect\n   trace equal the reference (law 1); the relift equals the lift by root\n   id under rows/canonical-under (law 2); the pending's reason is the\n   observed wait's (law 3); every lifted frame passes the validator\n   (law 6). Row 20 runs once, outside the wrappers.\n\n   Phase 6c adds the two de Bruijn lanes (§5.3): a world built under\n   *lane* :stack or :register runs A's derived image on that kernel and\n   lifts and lowers through yin.vm.semantic-register.layout. Law 4 (one\n   root id on all three lanes under canonical-under), law 5 (six ordered\n   lowering pairs, each continuing to the reference result) and the\n   layout refusals close the file.\"\n  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n            [dao.jing :as jing]\n            [dao.stream :as stream]\n            [dao.stream.apply :as apply2]\n            [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n            [yin.vm :as vm]\n            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n            [yin.vm.ffi :as ffi]\n            [yin.vm.module :as module]\n            [yin.vm.values :as values]\n            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register :as sr]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.register :as rvm]\n            [yin.vm.debruijn.stack :as dvm]\n            [yin.vm.parity-test :as b0]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.analysis :as analysis]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.code :as code]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.corpus :as corpus]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame :as frame]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.frame-test :as ft]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.layout :as layout]\n            [yin.vm.semantic-register.linearize :as linearize]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.lift-support :as support]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.rows :as rows]\n            [yin.vm.ucf.v2-support :as s]))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The composition: code by A, the source index, one machine builder\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(def source-index\n  \"The composition's {A #{tree-address}} (§6.1): every vector this\n   harness projects is recorded beside the address of its AST.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def code-index\n  \"{A v}: every vector this harness projects, for the layouts' spaces.\"\n  (atom {}))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *projected*\n  \"When bound, an atom {A v} of the vectors one world projected: the\n   layouts' spaces read it instead of the whole file's code-index, so an\n   alpha-equivalent A an unrelated fixture projected widens no lookup.\"\n  nil)\n\n\n(defn project\n  [ast]\n  (let [v (:vector (linearize/project ast))\n        a (jing/segment-key v)]\n    (swap! source-index update a (fnil conj #{}) (jing/segment-key [:yin/tree ast]))\n    (swap! code-index assoc a v)\n    (when *projected* (swap! *projected* assoc a v))\n    v))\n\n\n(defn scoped\n  \"f's result, every vector it projects recorded in a fresh *projected*.\"\n  [f]\n  (binding [*projected* (atom {})] (f)))\n\n\n(defn file-wide\n  \"f's result, the layouts' spaces reading every vector the file ever\n   projected: only the fixtures that show that contamination.\"\n  [f]\n  (binding [*projected* code-index] (f)))\n\n\n(def stream-modules (module/register-stream-module (module/default-registry)))\n\n\n(def ^:dynamic *lane*\n  \"The kernel a world is built on: :semantic-register (the reference\n   lane), or :stack or :register, which run A's derived image and lift\n   and lower through the layouts (§5.3).\"\n  :semantic-register)\n\n\n(def lanes [:semantic-register :stack :register])\n\n\n(defn- composition\n  [opts]\n  (merge {:make-stream tu/make-stream :capability-secret tu/secret\n          :secret-source (fn [origin] (str tu/secret \"/\" (name origin)))\n          :modules stream-modules}\n         opts))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-opts\n  \"A de Bruijn kernel's options for the same composition: the full\n   primitive table, and the initial environment as :free-env.\"\n  [opts]\n  (cond-> (assoc (dissoc (composition opts) :env) :primitives vm/primitives)\n    (contains? opts :env) (assoc :free-env (:env opts))))\n\n\n(defn machine\n  ([] (machine {}))\n  ([opts]\n   (case *lane*\n     :semantic-register (sr/create-vm (composition opts))\n     :stack (dvm/create-vm [] (kernel-opts opts))\n     :register (rvm/create-vm (assoc {} :bodies [] :instructions []) (kernel-opts opts)))))\n\n\n(defn lane-of\n  [m]\n  (let [f (:format (module/link-format m))]\n    (cond (= dvm/format-tag f) :stack\n          (= rvm/format-tag f) :register\n          :else :semantic-register)))\n\n\n(def segment-of\n  \"layout/segment, once per A.\"\n  (memoize layout/segment))\n\n\n(defn kernel-space\n  \"The layout space of the A vectors whose images de Bruijn kernel k\n   holds, among those this world projected (`scoped`), or the file ever\n   projected (`file-wide`). Unbound, it throws: an independent world's\n   lookups never read another fixture's vectors.\"\n  [k]\n  (when-not *projected*\n    (throw (ex-info \"kernel-space outside scoped or file-wide\" {})))\n  (let [id (if (= :stack (lane-of k)) :stack-id :register-id)\n        held (into #{} (map first) (:images k))]\n    (layout/space (filter #(contains? held (id %)) (map segment-of (vals @*projected*))))))\n\n\n(defn- kernel-load\n  \"Attach v's derived image and start it at its row, beside whatever the\n   kernel already holds: parked records keep naming their own rows.\"\n  [k v]\n  (let [kind (lane-of k)\n        sg (segment-of v)\n        k (if (= :stack kind)\n            (dvm/attach-image k (:stack sg) vm/stack-contract)\n            (rvm/attach-image k (:register sg) vm/register-contract))\n        k (assoc k :pc (layout/offset kind k sg) :frames [] :continuation [] :store-of nil\n                 :halted? false :blocked? false :value nil)]\n    (if (= :stack kind)\n      (assoc k :stack [])\n      (assoc k :registers (vec (repeat (:registers (first (:bodies (:register sg)))) nil))))))\n\n\n(defn load-program\n  [m ast]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (sr/load-vector m (project ast) code/contract)\n    (kernel-load m (project ast))))\n\n\n(defn lane-closure\n  \"Canonical closure payload c, its :segment an A, as machine m's value.\"\n  [m c]\n  (if (= :semantic-register (lane-of m))\n    (values/closure (:owner m) (update c :segment #(get (:code-aliases m) %)))\n    (layout/positional-value (layout/lower-context m (kernel-space m)) (values/closure (:owner m) c))))\n\n\n(defn lift-opts\n  []\n  {:source-index @source-index})\n\n\n(defn error\n  [f]\n  (try (f) nil (catch #?(:cljd Object :clj Throwable :cljs :default) e (ex-data e))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The corpus: four segments around one parking expression\n;; =============================================================================\n\n(defn cat-of\n  [p q]\n  (s/app (s/v 'cat) p q))\n\n\n(defn with-cat\n  [ast]\n  (s/let1 'cat (s/lam ['p 'q] (s/app (s/v 'conj) (s/v 'p) (s/v 'q))) ast))\n\n\n(defn nest\n  [d op]\n  (if (zero? d) op (cat-of (s/lit [d]) (s/app (s/lam ['x] (nest (dec d) op)) (s/lit d)))))\n\n\n(def segments\n  \"[label wrap expected-of-bare-result] (§5.2).\"\n  [[:bare identity identity]\n   [:operand #(cat-of (s/lit [:operand]) %) (fn [r] [:operand r])]\n   [:depth-3 #(nest 3 %) (fn [r] [3 [2 [1 r]]])]\n   [:captured #(s/let1 'k (s/lit :captured)\n                       (s/let1 'f (s/lam ['y] (cat-of (cat-of (cat-of (s/lit []) (s/v 'k)) (s/v 'y)) %))\n                               (s/app (s/v 'f) (s/lit :arg))))\n    (fn [r] [:captured :arg r])]])\n\n\n(defn with-stream\n  [body]\n  (s/let1 's {:type :stream/make :buffer 4} (s/let1 'c (s/cursor-of (s/v 's)) body)))\n\n\n(defn tail\n  [ast]\n  (assoc ast :tail? true))\n\n\n(defn normalize\n  [x]\n  (cond\n    (values/continuation? x) :continuation\n    (values/closure? x) :closure\n    (vector? x) (mapv normalize x)\n    (seq? x) (apply list (map normalize x))\n    (set? x) (into #{} (map normalize) x)\n    (map? x) (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [(normalize k) (normalize v)])) x)\n    :else x))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; The rows of §5.2: one builder each, answering the parked machine\n;; =============================================================================\n;;\n;; A world: :machine, :kind, :reason (blocked rows), :steps (each followed by\n;; a drive) or :resume, :finish (records the effect trace), :trace, and\n;; :receiver (fresh opts and a finish for the receiver's own composition).\n\n(defn reader\n  \"A reader parked on (next-of c); :pre values are appended and the\n   machine re-run first.\"\n  ([wrap op] (reader wrap op [] \"B\" {}))\n  ([wrap op pre value opts]\n   (let [m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine opts) (with-stream (with-cat (wrap op)))))\n         src (s/stream-of m0)\n         m (reduce (fn [m x] (stream/append! src x) (vm/run m)) m0 pre)]\n     {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :next :steps [#(stream/append! src value)] :trace (atom [])})))\n\n\n(defn writer\n  [wrap]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        w (support/one-slot-stream \"w\")\n        _ (stream/append! w :warmed)\n        m0 (load-program (machine) (with-cat (wrap {:type :stream/put :target (s/v 'w) :val (s/lit \"v\")})))\n        [ref m1] (engine/attach-resource m0 w)\n        take! #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next w 0)))]\n    {:machine (vm/run (assoc m1 :store {'w ref})) :kind :blocked :reason :put :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [take!] :finish take! :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn own-call-pair\n  [trace]\n  (let [own-in (s/ring 8) own-out (s/ring 8)]\n    {:opts {:call-in own-in :call-out own-out :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest own-out :test)}\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain own-in))}))\n\n\n(defn caller\n  [wrap call-in call-out]\n  (vm/run (load-program (machine {:call-in call-in :call-out call-out\n                                  :call-out-cursor (vm/mint-oldest call-out :test)})\n                        (with-cat (wrap (s/call-node :op/echo \"hello\"))))))\n\n\n(defn sent-ffi\n  [wrap]\n  (let [trace (atom []) call-in (s/ring 8) call-out (s/ring 8)\n        m (caller wrap call-in call-out)\n        id (ffi/response-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :ffi :call-id id\n     :steps [#(stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\"))]\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain call-in))\n     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace) :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn retained-ffi\n  [wrap]\n  (let [trace (atom []) call-in (support/one-slot-stream \"call-in\") call-out (s/ring 8)\n        _ (stream/append! call-in :warmed)\n        m (caller wrap call-in call-out)\n        id (ffi/request-call-id (first (:wait-set m)))]\n    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :ffi-request :surfaces #{:reader :writer}\n     :steps [#(stream/next call-in 0)\n             (fn []\n               (swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next call-in 0)))\n               (stream/append! call-out (apply2/success-response id \"echo!\")))]\n     :receiver #(own-call-pair trace) :trace trace}))\n\n\n(defn module-response\n  [body exports]\n  {:status :ok :image {:value (project body)}\n   :manifest {:yin.module/name 'host.mod :yin.module/exports exports} :obligations []})\n\n\n(def plain-body (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42))))\n\n\n(def blocking-body\n  \"host.mod's body reads a stream nothing feeds yet, then defines f. No\n   binding holds the stream, so f's E does not capture it.\"\n  (s/then (s/next-of (s/cursor-of {:type :stream/make :buffer 4})) (s/def! 'f (s/lam [] (s/lit 42)))))\n\n\n(defn require-op\n  [tail?]\n  (let [call (s/app (s/v 'require) (s/lit 'host.mod))]\n    (if tail? (s/app (s/lam ['u] (tail call)) (s/lit 0)) call)))\n\n\n(defn link-receiver\n  [trace]\n  (fn []\n    (let [rq (s/ring 64)]\n      {:opts {:link-request rq :link-response (s/ring 64)} :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain rq))})))\n\n\n(defn linking\n  \"A require parked in :link-response (or :link-request behind a full,\n   warmed request stream when retained?).\"\n  [wrap tail? retained?]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        request (if retained? (support/one-slot-stream \"link-request\") (s/ring 64))\n        response (s/ring 64)\n        _ (when retained? (stream/append! request :warmed))\n        m (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n                                (with-cat (wrap (require-op tail?)))))\n        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m)))\n        answer! #(stream/append! response (assoc (module-response plain-body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))]\n    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason (if retained? :link-request :link-response)\n     :surfaces #{:reader :writer} :trace trace\n     :steps (if retained? [#(stream/next request 0) answer!] [answer!])\n     :finish (if retained?\n               #(swap! trace conj (:dao.stream/value (stream/next request 0)))\n               #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request)))\n     :receiver (link-receiver trace)}))\n\n\n(defn installing\n  \"A require parked on :install beside its blocked child.\"\n  [wrap tail? phase]\n  (let [trace (atom [])\n        request (s/ring 64) response (s/ring 64)\n        m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n                                 (with-cat (wrap (require-op tail?)))))\n        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m0)))\n        _ (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response blocking-body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))\n        m1 (vm/run m0)\n        m (if phase (assoc-in m1 [:installs 'host.mod :phase] phase) m1)\n        child (get-in m [:installs 'host.mod :vm])\n        child-stream (s/stream-of child)]\n    {:machine m :kind :blocked :reason :install :trace trace\n     :steps [#(stream/append! child-stream :fed)]\n     :finish #(swap! trace into (tu/drain request))\n     :receiver (link-receiver trace)}))\n\n\n(defn module-context\n  \"Blocked inside host.mod's exported closure, whose E names store-of host.mod.\"\n  [wrap]\n  (let [request (s/ring 64) response (s/ring 64)\n        body (s/def! 'f (s/lam ['c] (s/app (s/v 'stream/next!) (s/v 'c))))\n        m0 (vm/run (load-program (machine {:link-request request :link-response response})\n                                 (with-stream (with-cat (wrap (s/then (s/app (s/v 'require) (s/lit 'host.mod))\n                                                                      (s/app (s/v 'host.mod/f) (s/v 'c))))))))\n        id (:link-id (first (:wait-set m0)))\n        _ (stream/append! response (assoc (module-response body #{'f}) :yin.link/id id))\n        m (vm/run m0)\n        src (s/stream-of m)]\n    ;; The carrier holds module stores, not registry entries: the receiver's\n    ;; composition links host.