{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LnsGn1CSnaiNpM5NLALYzt","type":"tool_result","content":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.custody\n  \"The custody facts of M-next C slice C5 (UCF 7.2.1, 7.7.2, 7.7.8): the\n   occurrence form, the offer and binding constructors with the\n   validators the ledger fold runs, and `binding-evidence`, the pure\n   reader-side proof that a grant carries a valid epoch binding.\n\n   An occurrence is a UUID string minted once at park, in its one\n   lowercase spelling, so two ids are equal exactly when their canonical\n   bytes are.  It is stable across retries because the emitter keeps it,\n   not because it is derived; it is distinct for distinct parks and\n   collision-resistant by its 122 random bits.\n\n   The authority records three fact kinds here, beside C3's:\n     :yin.k/offered       an admitted offer of one snapshot variant, with\n                          the operation baseline the inspector derived\n     :dao.lease/accepted  the lease grant, the dao.lease fact unchanged\n     :yin.k/bound         the grant's epoch binding, in the same\n                          transaction as its grant\n\n   Nothing here throws on any input.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n\n\n(def max-exact\n  \"2^52-1, the largest epoch (7.7.8).\"\n  4503599627370495)\n\n\n(defn exact?\n  \"A nonnegative exact integer no greater than 2^52-1, by the canonical\n   codec's integer kind: an integral float is not one.\"\n  [x]\n  (and (cbor/numeric? x)\n       (= :integer (cbor/numeric-kind x))\n       (not (neg? (cbor/num-compare x 0)))\n       (not (pos? (cbor/num-compare x max-exact)))))\n\n\n;; =============================================================================\n;; Occurrence\n29:(defn exact?\n30-  \"A nonnegative exact integer no greater than 2^52-1, by the canonical\n31-   codec's integer kind: an integral float is not one.\"\n32-  [x]\n33-  (and (cbor/numeric? x)\n34-       (= :integer (cbor/numeric-kind x))\n35-       (not (neg? (cbor/num-compare x 0)))\n36-       (not (pos? (cbor/num-compare x max-exact)))))\n37-\n--\n49:(defn occurrence?\n50-  \"True for an occurrence id: a UUID string in lowercase hex.\"\n51-  [x]\n52-  (and (string? x)\n53-       (some? (re-matches\n54-                #\"[0-9a-f]{8}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{4}-[0-9a-f]{12}\"\n55-                x))))\n56-\n57-\n                                           (portable-frame m (ft/canonical m (values/payload x) false)) encoded))])}\n    (values/closure? x)\n    (let [p (values/payload x) e (:env p)]\n      {:yin.k/row (rows/node :closure [(get-in m [:code (:segment p) :address]) (:entry p) (:params p)\n                                       (rows/node :bindings\n                                                  (mapcat (fn [[k v]] [k (encoded (portable-value m v))])\n                                                          (sort #(cbor/encoded-compare (first %1) (first %2))\n                                                                (engine/without-store-of e))))\n                                       (engine/env-store-of e)])})\n    (fn? x) {:yin.k/row (rows/node :prim ['fixture/primitive])}\n    (and (map? x) (= :cursor-ref (:type x))) {:yin.k/cursor-cell (:id x)}\n    (and (map? x) (= :stream-ref (:type x))) {:yin.k/row (rows/node :stream [(:id x) :fixture/served])}\n    (coll? x)\n    (let [kind (cond (map? x) :map (vector? x) :vec (set? x) :set :else :list)\n          xs (if (map? x) (mapcat identity x) x)\n          vs (mapv #(encoded (portable-value m %)) xs)]\n      (if (some #(not= :lit (first %)) vs)\n        {:yin.k/row (rows/node kind vs)}\n        x))\n    :else x))\n\n\n(defn portable-frame\n  [m f]\n  (let [bindings (fn [mappings] (into {} (map (fn [[k v]] [k (portable-value m v)])) mappings))\n        env #(update % :yin.k/bindings bindings)]\n    (cond-> (update f :yin.k/k #(mapv (fn [k]\n                                        (-> k (update :yin.k/env env)\n                                            (update :yin.k/window bindings))) %))\n      (= :act (:yin.k/state f)) (update :yin.k/env env)\n      (= :act (:yin.k/state f)) (update :yin.k/window bindings)\n      (contains? f :yin.k/pending) (update :yin.k/pending #(case (:yin.k/reason %)\n                                                             :next (assoc % :yin.k/cursor-cell :test/cursor)\n                                                             :put (assoc % :yin.k/stream (rows/node :stream [:fixture/w :fixture/served])\n                                                                         :yin.k/value \"v\" :yin.k/op-id nil) %)))))\n\n\n(deftest bijection\n  (doseq [fixture (ft/reference-machines)\n          {:keys [frame]} (ft/reference-frames fixture)]\n    (let [f (portable-frame (:machine fixture) frame) wire (rows/frame->rows f encoded) back (rows/rows->frame wire)]\n      (is (= f back))\n      (is (= (:yin.k/root wire) (:yin.k/root (rows/frame->rows back encoded)))))))\n\n\n(deftest row-ids-are-jing-default\n  (let [wire (rows/emit (fixture :stream/a :stream/b :source/x :source/y))]\n    (is (seq (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n    (doseq [[id & body] (:yin.k/rows wire)]\n      (is (= id (jing/segment-key (vec body))))\n      (is (= :blake3 (:algorithm (jing/parse-segment-address id)))))))\n\n\n(defn- replace-row\n  \"Rehash the edited row and all ancestors, without canonicalizing slots.\"\n  [wire id body]\n  (let [index (into {} (map (fn [r] [(first r) r])) (:yin.k/rows wire))\n        memo (atom {})]\n    (letfn [(rewrite\n              [x]\n              (cond\n                (contains? index x)\n                (or (get @memo x)\n                    (let [rbody (if (= x id) body (subvec (get index x) 1))\n                          b (mapv rewrite rbody) nid (jing/segment-key b)]\n                      (swap! memo assoc x nid)\n                      nid))\n                (vector? x) (mapv rewrite x)\n                :else x))]\n      (let [root (rewrite (:yin.k/root wire))\n            rs (mapv (fn [[old new]] (into [new] (mapv rewrite (if (= old id) body (subvec (get index old) 1))))) @memo)]\n        (assoc wire :yin.k/root root :yin.k/rows rs)))))\n\n\n(deftest window-sorted-and-unique\n  (let [f (assoc ft/worked-frame :yin.k/window {1 :f 3 nil})\n        wire (rows/frame->rows f) r (first (filter #(= :window (second %)) (:yin.k/rows wire)))\n        id (first r)]\n    (doseq [body [[:window 3 [:lit nil] 1 [:lit :f]] [:window 1 [:lit :f] 1 [:lit nil]]]]\n      (let [d (error #(rows/rows->frame (replace-row wire id body)))]\n        (is (= :yin.k/undecodable (:yin.k/status d)))","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e6ad7c4d-4e91-4daf-807a-5f71c598506b","uuid":"0532d14d-da4c-4611-84a3-edd38675a93b","timestamp":"2026-10-13T09:21:43.091Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"(ns yin.vm.ucf.custody\n  \"The custody facts of M-next C slice C5 (UCF 7.2.1, 7.7.2, 7.7.8): the\n   occurrence form, the offer and binding constructors with the\n   validators the ledger fold runs, and `binding-evidence`, the pure\n   reader-side proof that a grant carries a valid epoch binding.\n\n   An occurrence is a UUID string minted once at park, in its one\n   lowercase spelling, so two ids are equal exactly when their canonical\n   bytes are.  It is stable across retries because the emitter keeps it,\n   not because it is derived; it is distinct for distinct parks and\n   collision-resistant by its 122 random bits.\n\n   The authority records three fact kinds here, beside C3's:\n     :yin.k/offered       an admitted offer of one snapshot variant, with\n                          the operation baseline the inspector derived\n     :dao.lease/accepted  the lease grant, the dao.lease fact unchanged\n     :yin.k/bound         the grant's epoch binding, in the same\n                          transaction as its grant\n\n   Nothing here throws on any input.\"\n  (:require [dao.jing.cbor :as cbor]))\n\n\n(def max-exact\n  \"2^52-1, the larges