  :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])\n          :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)\n          (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))))))\n\n\n(defn lower-task\n  \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the\n   receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,\n   then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,\n   primitives) and custody, each step over the whole tree before the\n   next, all before the first attach! (step 11); then restore (step 12),\n   which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the restored machine,\n   or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"\n  ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))\n  ([recv wire attach! opts]\n   (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]\n     (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))\n     ;; each step over the whole tree before the next (§3.3)\n     (doseq [step [check-stores! check-pendings! check-dependencies! check-custody!]\n             [t role] (task-tree task :root)]\n       (step recv t role))\n     (restore-task recv task (attach-streams! attach! task)))))\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":2184,"oldLines":26,"newStart":2184,"newLines":35,"lines":["             machine (assoc base :store store' :module-stores stores :parked parked' :installs installs'","                            :resources resources :env fe :free-env fe :window {} :k nil :control nil","                            :ready-queue [] :id-counter (max (or (:id-counter base) 0) id-counter))]","-        (case kind","-          :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])","-          :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)","-          (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))))))","+        (with-custody","+          (case kind","+            :halted (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (value result) :wait-set [])","+            :parked (assoc machine :halted? true :blocked? false :value (get parked' parked-id) :wait-set entries)","+            (assoc machine :halted? false :blocked? true :value :yin/blocked :wait-set entries))","+          custody kind root?)))))"," "," "," (defn lower-task","   \"The lower of §7.2 into recv, a fresh semantic-register machine of the","    receiver's composition: gate to frames (decode) and the store keys,","    then pendings and install records, dependency closure (code, closures,","-   primitives) and custody, each step over the whole tree before the","-   next, all before the first attach! (step 11); then restore (step 12),","-   which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the restored machine,","-   or throws the first refusal as ex-data.\"","+   primitives), each step over the whole tree before the next, then","+   custody (check-custody!), all before the first attach! (step 11); then","+   restore (step 12), which therefore meets no carrier defect. Answers the","+   restored machine, or throws the first refusal as ex-data.","+   opts: :budget; :exclusive, refuse a fork root; :grant and :protection,","+   required by a blocked or parked exclusive root (handoff.cljc's reader","+   contract: the grant names :checkpoint, the pack address, its lease,","+   holder, tenure and evidence; :protection maps every stream identity of","+   the tree to its class); :fenced, an administrative rehydration that","+   skips the grant.\"","   ([recv wire attach!] (lower-task recv wire attach! {}))","   ([recv wire attach! opts]","    (let [task (decode wire (merge default-budget (:budget opts)))]","      (when-not (= :task (:kind task)) (outcome! :yin.k/undecodable :root {}))","      ;; each step over the whole tree bef